query:
IF/ELSEIF/ELSE (and CASE/WHEN/ELSE) that returns on every branch is incorrectly rejected as missing a RETURN

### Description

`SqlRoutineAnalyzer.validateReturn` only checks whether the *literal last statement* of a function body is a `RETURN`:

https://github.com/trinodb/trino/blob/master/core/trino-main/src/main/java/io/trino/sql/routine/SqlRoutineAnalyzer.java#L359-L370

```java
private static void validateReturn(ControlStatement statement)
{
    switch (statement) {
        case ReturnStatement _ -> {}
        case CompoundStatement body -> {
            if (!(getLast(body.getStatements(), null) instanceof ReturnStatement)) {
                throw semanticException(MISSING_RETURN, body, "Function must end in a RETURN statement");
            }
        }
        default -> throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid function statement: " + statement);
    }
}
```

It doesn't recurse into `IfStatement`/`CaseStatement` branches, so a function whose `IF`/`ELSEIF`/`ELSE` (or `CASE`/`WHEN`/`ELSE`) returns on every branch is rejected, even though every possible path through it does return.

This affects Trino's own documented example (https://trino.io/docs/current/udf/sql/if.html):

```sql
FUNCTION simple_if(a bigint)
  RETURNS varchar
  BEGIN
    IF a = 0 THEN
      RETURN 'zero';
    ELSEIF a = 1 THEN
      RETURN 'one';
    ELSE
      RETURN 'more than one or negative';
    END IF;
  END
```

### Steps to reproduce

```sql
WITH FUNCTION simple_if(a bigint) RETURNS varchar
BEGIN
  IF a = 0 THEN
    RETURN 'zero';
  ELSEIF a = 1 THEN
    RETURN 'one';
  ELSE
    RETURN 'more than one or negative';
  END IF;
END
SELECT simple_if(3);
```

### Expected behavior

The query runs and returns `more than one or negative`.

### Actual behavior

```
Query failed: line 2:1: Function must end in a RETURN statement
```

verbatim from the docs example, which cannot currently be run as written.

### Additional context

I ran into this while adding `sqlglot` support for Trino's inline SQL UDF `IF` statement and testing round-trips against a real Trino instance. I have a fix ready (extending the check to recurse into `IfStatement`/`CaseStatement` branches when an `ELSE` is present) and will open a PR shortly.

