I reproduced this on current `master` using the query from this issue. The failure is caused by `MERGE` coalescing independently generated target and source row IDs before `MarkDistinct`. Those independent ID namespaces can contain the same numeric value, which makes unrelated rows look like duplicate matches.

I opened #30937 to retain the row-ID origin in the distinct key. The regression test fails with `MERGE_TARGET_ROW_MULTIPLE_MATCHES` before the planner change and passes afterward. The existing test for genuine multiple source matches also still passes.

