query:
Delta Lake checkpoint writer drops files with deletion vectors when add precedes remove in a commit

Trino-written checkpoints key `add` and `remove` actions by `path` only, while the Delta protocol identifies a logical file by `(path, deletionVector.uniqueId)` ([Action Reconciliation](https://github.com/delta-io/delta/blob/master/PROTOCOL.md#action-reconciliation)). When a commit written by another engine lists `add(path, dv)` before `remove(path, no dv)` for the same data file, `CheckpointBuilder` replays the commit in file order and the `remove` erases the `add`. The next checkpoint Trino writes no longer contains the file, so every reader that starts from `_last_checkpoint` silently loses its rows.

`CheckpointBuilder.handleRemoveFileEntry` does `addFileEntries.remove(entry.path())` and `handleAddFileEntry` does `removeFileEntries.remove(entry.path())`. Log replay in `TransactionLogAccess.activeAddEntries` already uses the `(path, dvId)` key, so queries are correct until Trino writes a checkpoint.

Spark writes DV deletes in exactly this order. The repository already contains such a table at `plugin/trino-delta-lake/src/test/resources/deltalake/deletion_vector_pages`, whose `00000000000000000002.json` is `add(part-00000-8e78760d..., dv)`, `remove(part-00000-8e78760d...)`, `add(part-00000-2007aafe...)`.

### Steps to reproduce

Run against a `delta` catalog with a local file system (for example `TestDeltaLakeBasic` setup), after copying `deltalake/deletion_vector_pages` from test resources to `<location>`:

```sql
CALL system.register_table('tpch', 'dv_checkpoint', '<location>');
SELECT count(*) FROM dv_checkpoint;                -- 20001
-- 8 commits take the table from version 2 to version 10, the default checkpoint interval
INSERT INTO dv_checkpoint VALUES -1;               -- repeat 8 times
SELECT count(*) FROM dv_checkpoint;                -- 9
```

`_delta_log` now contains `00000000000000000010.checkpoint.parquet` without the `part-00000-8e78760d...` add entry. The 20000 live rows of that file are gone for any reader of the checkpoint.

Verified on `b9d32772206` (branch of #30343) with this test body added to `TestDeltaLakeBasic`:

```java
String tableName = "dv_checkpoint" + randomNameSuffix();
Path tableLocation = catalogDir.resolve(tableName);
copyDirectoryContents(new File(Resources.getResource("deltalake/deletion_vector_pages").toURI()).toPath(), tableLocation);
assertUpdate("CALL system.register_table('%s', '%s', '%s')".formatted(getSession().getSchema().orElseThrow(), tableName, tableLocation.toUri()));
assertThat(computeScalar("SELECT count(*) FROM " + tableName)).isEqualTo(20001L);
for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
    assertUpdate("INSERT INTO " + tableName + " VALUES -1", 1);
}
assertThat(computeScalar("SELECT count(*) FROM " + tableName)).isEqualTo(20009L); // actual: 9
```

### Expected

`CheckpointBuilder` should key file actions by `(path, deletionVector.uniqueId)` like `TransactionLogAccess.activeAddEntries` does, so the checkpoint keeps the `add` with the deletion vector.

