Iceberg: equality delete keyed on a field nested in a row column deletes all older rows in the partition (key read as NULL)

## Summary

When an equality delete file's `equality_ids` include a field that lives **inside a `row` column** (for example `root.nested`), Trino reads the delete key as `NULL` on both the delete-file side and the data-file side. Every row then matches the same `(NULL, ...)` key, so **any equality delete file removes all rows with a lower data sequence number in the partition**, not only the rows whose keys it lists. The query silently returns only the newest commit's rows. There is no error.

Seen on a v2 table (Parquet, Hive metastore) written by the Apache Iceberg Kafka Connect sink in upsert mode. Each commit adds a data file, an equality delete file for the keys in that batch, and a position delete file for superseded copies within the batch.

## Observed

On a real table, one partition holds about 21,300 live rows. Apache Spark reads the same snapshots and returns 21,302 / 21,305 / 21,305 / 21,305 at four successive commits. Trino 481 returned 461 / 465 / 424 / 507, roughly the size of the newest batch only. I checked Spark's numbers independently by applying the Iceberg v2 delete rules (position deletes, plus equality deletes to strictly older data) to the raw Parquet files, and they agree with Spark. I saw the same result on a 483-based build; I have not yet checked current `master`.

## Reproduction

The test below uses the Iceberg API to write files the way an upsert sink does. Three commits with overlapping key ranges: each commit adds a data file (two versions per key), an equality delete for its keys (equality ids = `root.nested` and `tag`), and a position delete removing the older version. The correct live row count is the union of the keys.

Expected `2000`, actual `1000`. It fails at any size I tried (10, 100 and 1000 keys per commit) and with or without position deletes. It passes only when each delete file names a single key, which is why the existing nested-key tests don't catch it.

<details>
<summary>Test and helper (added to <code>TestIcebergV2</code>)</summary>

```java
    @Test
    public void testUpsertBatchesWithOverlappingKeys()
            throws Exception
    {
        // Each commit upserts many keys, writing every key twice (older copy removed by a position delete) plus an
        // equality delete per key; commits overlap on part of their key ranges, so only the overlap is replaced
        try (TestTable table = newTrinoTable("test_upsert_overlapping_keys_", "(id BIGINT, root ROW(nested VARCHAR), tag VARCHAR) WITH (partitioning = ARRAY['tag'])")) {
            String tableName = table.getName();
            Table icebergTable = loadTable(tableName);
            commitUpsertKeys(icebergTable, keyRange(0, 1000));
            commitUpsertKeys(icebergTable, keyRange(500, 1500));
            commitUpsertKeys(icebergTable, keyRange(1000, 2000));

            assertThat(query("SELECT count(*) FROM " + tableName))
                    .matches("VALUES BIGINT '2000'");
            assertThat(query("SELECT count(DISTINCT root.nested) FROM " + tableName))
                    .matches("VALUES BIGINT '2000'");
            assertThat(query("SELECT count(*) FROM " + tableName + " WHERE root.nested IN ('k0', 'k700', 'k1200', 'k1999')"))
                    .matches("VALUES BIGINT '4'");
        }
    }

    private static List<String> keyRange(int fromInclusive, int toExclusive)
    {
        ImmutableList.Builder<String> keys = ImmutableList.builder();
        for (int i = fromInclusive; i < toExclusive; i++) {
            keys.add("k" + i);
        }
        return keys.build();
    }

    private void commitUpsertKeys(Table icebergTable, List<String> keys)
            throws IOException
    {
        FileIO fileIo = FILE_IO_FACTORY.create(fileSystemFactory.create(SESSION));
        Schema schema = icebergTable.schema();
        PartitionData partition = new PartitionData(new Object[] {"x"});

        DataWriter<Record> dataWriter = Parquet.writeData(fileIo.newOutputFile("local:///data_file_" + UUID.randomUUID() + ".parquet"))
                .forTable(icebergTable)
                .withSpec(icebergTable.spec())
                .withPartition(partition)
                .createWriterFunc(GenericParquetWriter::create)
                .overwrite()
                .build();
        try (Closeable ignored = dataWriter) {
            long id = 0;
            for (String key : keys) {
                for (int version = 0; version < 2; version++) {
                    Record root = GenericRecord.create(schema.findField("root").type().asStructType());
                    root.setField("nested", key);
                    Record row = GenericRecord.create(schema);
                    row.setField("id", id++);
                    row.setField("root", root);
                    row.setField("tag", "x");
                    dataWriter.write(row);
                }
            }
        }
        DataFile dataFile = dataWriter.toDataFile();

        Schema deleteSchema = schema.select("root.nested", "tag");
        EqualityDeleteWriter<Record> equalityDeleteWriter = Parquet.writeDeletes(fileIo.newOutputFile("local:///equality_delete_" + UUID.randomUUID() + ".parquet"))
                .forTable(icebergTable)
                .rowSchema(deleteSchema)
                .withSpec(icebergTable.spec())
                .withPartition(partition)
                .createWriterFunc(GenericParquetWriter::create)
                .equalityFieldIds(deleteSchema.findField("root.nested").fieldId(), deleteSchema.findField("tag").fieldId())
                .overwrite()
                .buildEqualityWriter();
        try (Closeable ignored = equalityDeleteWriter) {
            for (String key : keys) {
                Record root = GenericRecord.create(deleteSchema.findField("root").type().asStructType());
                root.setField("nested", key);
                Record deleteKey = GenericRecord.create(deleteSchema);
                deleteKey.setField("root", root);
                deleteKey.setField("tag", "x");
                equalityDeleteWriter.write(deleteKey);
            }
        }

        PositionDeleteWriter<Record> positionDeleteWriter = Parquet.writeDeletes(fileIo.newOutputFile("local:///position_delete_" + UUID.randomUUID() + ".parquet"))
                .createWriterFunc(GenericParquetWriter::create)
                .withSpec(icebergTable.spec())
                .withPartition(partition)
                .overwrite()
                .buildPositionWriter();
        try (Closeable ignored = positionDeleteWriter) {
            for (int i = 0; i < keys.size(); i++) {
                positionDeleteWriter.write(PositionDelete.<Record>create().set(dataFile.location(), 2L * i, null));
            }
        }

        icebergTable.newRowDelta()
                .addRows(dataFile)
                .addDeletes(equalityDeleteWriter.toDeleteFile())
                .addDeletes(positionDeleteWriter.toDeleteFile())
                .commit();
    }
